{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mcporter call exa.web_search_exa query='site:forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support \\\"CALENDAR:READ\\\" \\\"CALENDAR:WRITE\\\" invalid_request scopes' numResults=5\"","aggregated_output":"Title: Intervals.icu OAuth support\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n## Requesting Authorization To Access Intervals.icu Data For A User\n\nSend the user to:\n\n```auto\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=<your client id>\n    &redirect_uri=<your redirect uri>\n    &scope=<required scopes>\n    &state=<optional data>\n\n```\n\nIntervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which\nscopes to grant the application. If the user confirms then they are redirected to the redirect_uri with an\nauthorization code and the optional state parameter:\n\n```auto\n<your redirect uri>?code=3983ed415f66413c890ca48b7cce59e4&state=...\n\n```\n\nIf they decline:\n\n```auto\n<your redirect uri>?error=access_denied\n\n```\n\n...\n\nthe ... access ... id\n\n...\n\n/\n\n...\n\n\\\n\n...\n\n41 ... 4 ... 9\n\n...\n\nIf all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete:\n\n```auto\n{\n    \"token_type\": \"Bearer\",\n    \"access_token\": \"d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9\",\n    \"scope\": \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:WRITE\",\n    \"athlete\": {\n        \"id\": \"2049151\",\n        \"name\": \"David (intervals.icu)\"\n    }\n}   \n\n```\n\n...\n\nTo call the API use “Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9” header.\n\n...\n\n## Scopes\n\nScopes are as follows:\n\n- ACTIVITY: Completed rides, runs etc.\n- WELLNESS: Weight, resting HR etc.\n- CALENDAR: Planned workouts\n- CHATS: Chats, groups and messages\n- LIBRARY: Workout library\n- SETTINGS: Athlete settings\n\nFor each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. Example:\n\n```auto\nACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE\n\n```\n\nRequests read access to activities and read and write access to wellness data.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=3\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nHi David!\n\n...\n\nCan I ask a question re Scopes? If I want to read athlete data (get /api/v1/athlete/{id}) and gear data (get /api/v1/athlete/{id}/gear{ext}), what scope do I need?\n\nI tried “ATHLETE:READ,GEAR:READ”, but neither exists.\n\nCheers,\nJan\n\n---\n\nAuthor: @david\nPost date: 24 August 2025 18:07 UTC\n\nThese are the scopes: ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, LIBRARY, SETTINGS\n\nYou need SETTINGS:READ for those.\n\n...\n\nThere isn’t an endpoint to get an individual bit of gear. You need to use the one that lists all gear for the athlete:\n\n```\nGET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/gear{ext}\n\n```\n\nYou can pass 0 for the athlete id.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Page 2 - Announcements - Intervals.icu Forum\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=2\nPublished: 2022-08-30T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nI just implemented that. There can be many access tokens for an athlete linked to an app, once for each time they authorise it. The most recent scopes apply to all access tokens.\n\n...\n\nCurrently oauth ... to the ... ising athlete’s data but ... people ... or ... This ... by design so ... who follows you can’t auth a 3 ... party app which then gains access to your data. ... think you need to ... each athlete to auth your app and then use the correct ... depending on ... athlete.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - #7 by david - Announcements - Intervals.icu Forum\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759/7\nPublished: 2021-01-30T14:51:05.000Z\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n# Intervals.icu OAuth support\n\ndavid 7 September 2021 04:31 7\n\nCool. Its quite simple really: Just construct correct URL to send users to Intervals.icu to auth, then swap the code that comes back via the redirect URL for an access token.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
